    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 1016 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near Urich, or 11 miles northwest of Clinton, moving southeast at 30 mph. HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Locations impacted include... Clinton, Windsor, Urich, Calhoun, Deepwater, Coal, Brownington, Blairstown, Hartwell, La Due, and Truman Lake.",
